1
00:00:08,823 --> 00:00:14,823
One man. Countless myths. And in between lies the truth.

2
00:00:17,647 --> 00:00:23,647
Before the End: Searching for Jim Morrison is a
documentary film directed by Jeff Finn.

3
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:32,470
Documentary film about the iconic 1960s-era poet,
songwriter, and vocalist of the Doors.

4
00:00:35,294 --> 00:00:41,294
Unlike prior Morrison media, Before the End’s focus is on the
humanity behind the hype, including Jim’s formative years.

5
00:00:44,117 --> 00:00:50,117
The documentary features exclusive interviews with his brother, Andy Morrison; cousins Ellen Edwards and David Backer; high school swim coach, Ash Jones; college roommate, Bryan Gates; Doors-era
lovers Judy Huddleston and Anne Moore; Doors booking agent, Todd Schiffman; Doors roadie, Gareth Blyth; and the first appearance by Jim’s Paris-era personal assistant, Robyn Wurtele.

6
00:00:52,941 --> 00:00:58,941
Self (archive footage), played by Jim Morrison.

7
00:01:01,764 --> 00:01:07,764
Self (archive footage), played by Robby Krieger.

8
00:01:10,588 --> 00:01:16,588
Self (archive footage), played by Ray Manzarek.

9
00:01:19,411 --> 00:01:25,411
Self (archive footage), played by John Densmore.

10
00:01:28,235 --> 00:01:34,235
Self, played by Andy Morrison.

11
00:01:37,058 --> 00:01:43,058
Self (archive footage), played by Anne Morrison Chewning.

12
00:01:45,882 --> 00:01:51,882
Superman is a 2025 American superhero film based on
the eponymous character from DC Comics.

13
00:01:54,705 --> 00:02:00,705
Written and directed by James Gunn, it is the first film in the DC
Universe (DCU) and a reboot of the Superman film series.

14
00:02:03,529 --> 00:02:09,529
David Corenswet stars as Kal-El / Clark Kent / Superman, alongside Rachel Brosnahan,
Nicholas Hoult, Edi Gathegi, Anthony Carrigan, Nathan Fillion, and Isabela Merced.

15
00:02:12,352 --> 00:02:18,352
In the film, Superman faces unintended consequences after he intervenes in an
international conflict orchestrated by billionaire Lex Luthor (Hoult).

16
00:02:21,176 --> 00:02:27,176
Superman must win back public support with the help of
his reporter and superhero colleagues.

17
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The film was produced by Gunn and Peter Safran of DC Studios.

18
00:02:38,823 --> 00:02:44,823
Development on a sequel to the DC Extended Universe (DCEU) film Man of Steel (2013)
began by October 2014, with Henry Cavill set to return as Superman.

19
00:02:47,647 --> 00:02:53,647
Plans changed after the troubled production of Justice League (2017), and the
Man of Steel sequel was no longer moving forward by May 2020.

20
00:02:56,470 --> 00:03:02,470
Gunn began work on a new Superman film around August 2022.

21
00:03:05,294 --> 00:03:11,294
In October, he became co-CEO of DC Studios with Safran,
and they began work on a new DC Universe.

22
00:03:14,117 --> 00:03:20,117
Gunn was publicly revealed to be writing the film in December.

23
00:03:22,941 --> 00:03:28,941
The title Superman: Legacy was announced the next month; Gunn was confirmed to direct in
March 2023; and Corenswet and Brosnahan (Lois Lane) were cast that June.

24
00:03:31,764 --> 00:03:37,764
The subtitle was dropped by the end of February 2024,
when filming began in Svalbard, Norway.

25
00:03:40,588 --> 00:03:46,588
Production primarily took place at Trilith Studios in Atlanta,
Georgia, with location filming around Georgia and Ohio.

26
00:03:49,411 --> 00:03:55,411
Filming wrapped in July.

27
00:03:58,235 --> 00:04:04,235
The film's influences include the comic book All-Star Superman
(2005–2008) by Grant Morrison and Frank Quitely.

28
00:04:07,058 --> 00:04:13,058
Superman premiered at the TCL Chinese Theater on July 7,
2025, and was released by Warner Bros.

29
00:04:15,882 --> 00:04:21,882
Pictures in the United States on July 11.

30
00:04:24,705 --> 00:04:30,705
It is the first film in the DCU's Chapter One: Gods and Monsters.

31
00:04:33,529 --> 00:04:39,529
The film grossed $617 million worldwide, making it the tenth
highest-grossing film of 2025, and received mostly positive reviews.

32
00:04:42,352 --> 00:04:48,352
Critics found it to be fun, colorful, and earnest, although some felt it was overstuffed,
while the performances of Corenswet, Brosnahan, and Hoult were praised.

33
00:04:51,176 --> 00:04:57,176
A follow-up film, Man of Tomorrow, is scheduled for release in 2027, while a spin-off television series featuring
supporting characters from the film, including Skyler Gisondo's Jimmy Olsen, is in development for HBO Max.
